    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nThe determinant of a general [MATH: 2 \\times 2] matrix\n[MATH: [a|b; c|d]]\nis denoted [MATH: \\text {det} ({A})] and computed as\n[MATH: a|b; c|d]\n\nContent:\nFor example, given the matrix\n[MATH: [2|1; 5|3]]\nthe determinant is\n[MATH: \\det(A) = {\\color{blue}{2}} \\cdot {\\color{blue}{3}} - {\\color{red}{1}} \\cdot {\\color{red}{5}} = 1.]\n\nContent:\nTo remember how to compute the determinant of a [MATH: 2 \\times 2] matrix, you can imagine taking the product of the diagonal of the matrix, and then subtracting the product of the off-diagonal terms, as follows:\n\nGraphic:\n[IMG: /graphics/fa64b649b848e4196e7a4763e7a9e1f6]\n\nContent:\nLater, we will see that the determinant is related to the \"volume\" spanned by the row vectors or column vectors in a matrix. We will also see that the determinant can tell us about many other properties of a matrix.\n\nContent:\nHowever, in this lesson, we will just focus on computing the determinant.\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Calculating the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix With Integer Entries\n\nExample Prompt:\nCalculate [MATH: \\det(A),] if [MATH: [3|2; 5|6]]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFor a [MATH: 2 \\times 2] matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n[MATH: |a|b; c|d|]\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n[MATH: det(A)|=|3|2; 5|6|; = 3 \u22c5 6 \u2212 2 \u22c5 5; = 18 \u2212 10; = 8]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: |2|\u2212 4; \u2212 2|7|=]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: \u2212 6]\nb. [MATH: \u2212 4]\nc. [MATH: 1]\nd. [MATH: 4]\ne. [MATH: 6]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\nCalculate [MATH: det(A)], if\n[MATH: A = [1|2; 3|0].]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: \u2212 6]\nb. [MATH: 6]\nc. [MATH: 0]\nd. [MATH: \u2212 1]\ne. [MATH: 1]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Calculating the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix With Non-Integer Entries\n\nExample Prompt:\nCalculate [MATH: \\det(A),] if [MATH: [sqrt(2)|\u2212 2; 0|sqrt(3)]]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFor a [MATH: 2 \\times 2] matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n[MATH: |a|b; c|d|]\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n[MATH: det(A)|=|sqrt(2)|\u2212 2; 0|sqrt(3)|; = sqrt(2) \u22c5 sqrt(3) \u2212 (\u2212 2) \u22c5 0; = sqrt(6)]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\nCalculate [MATH: det(Z)], if\n[MATH: Z = [sqrt(x)|y; y^{2}|sqrt(x)].]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: x \u2212 y^{3}]\nb. [MATH: x \u2212 2y^{2}]\nc. [MATH: x \u2212 y^{2}]\nd. [MATH: sqrt(x) \u2212 2y^{3}]\ne. [MATH: 2sqrt(x) \u2212 y^{3}]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: |sqrt(2)|5; 1|3|=]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: sqrt(6) + 5]\nb. [MATH: 3sqrt(2) \u2212 5]\nc. [MATH: \u2212 2]\nd. [MATH: 1]\ne. [MATH: sqrt(6) \u2212 5]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Example: Solving for an Unknown in an Expression Involving the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix\n\nExample Prompt:\nIf\n[MATH: {A} =\n\\left\\lbrack\n\\matrix {\n2 & -1 \\\n-3 & k\n}\n\\right\\rbrack]\nand\n[MATH: \\det({A}) = 5], what is the value of [MATH: k?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFor a [MATH: 2 \\times 2] matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n[MATH: |a|b; c|d|]\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n[MATH: det(A)|=|2|\u2212 1; \u2212 3|k|; = 2 \u22c5 k \u2212 (\u2212 1) \u22c5 (\u2212 3); = 2k \u2212 3]\n\nSince [MATH: \\det(A)=5,] we obtain:\n\n[MATH: det(A)|= 5; 2k \u2212 3|= 5; 2k|= 8; k|= 4]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\nIf\n[MATH: A = [1 + t|2t; \u2212 3|1 \u2212 t]]\nand [MATH: det(A) = 10], what is the value of [MATH: t?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 3]\nb. [MATH: 2]\nc. [MATH: 1]\nd. [MATH: \u2212 3]\ne. [MATH: \u2212 1]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\nIf\n[MATH: C = [2|3; 5|k]]\nand\n[MATH: det(C) = 3], what is the value of [MATH: k?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: k = 4]\nb. [MATH: k = 9]\nc. [MATH: k = \u2212 9]\nd. [MATH: k = \u2212 4]\ne. [MATH: k = 0]"
  }
